    "updated_at": "2023-07-25T19:26:50Z",
    "body": "I made https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/9558 to handle the \"matches about:blank\" side of this issue, but after evaluating whether we should use \"matches about:srcdoc\" more often, I've tentatively determined the answer is no. Consider the following places where [\"about:srcdoc\"](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#about:srcdoc) definition:\r\n 1. [Navigate to \"about:srcdoc\"](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#the-iframe-element:about:srcdoc) in the iframe processing model: **N/A**\r\n 2. [determine navigation params policy container](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#policy-containers:about:srcdoc)\r\n    - This is called for (a) the response-is-non-null navigation case, (b) the about:srcdoc navigation case, and (c) the usual create navigation params by fetching case. The first two will never rely on the \"matches about:srcdoc\" distinction, and the latter doesn't apply for about:srcdoc navigations at all, so **\"no\" is my answer** to this one\r\n 4. [determine the origin](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#creating-browsing-contexts:about:srcdoc):\r\n    - Almost the **same as the above**. No uses rely on the distinction the new definition provides, due to either being used directly in the synthetic `about:srcdoc` response case, the response-is-non-null case, or create nav params by fetching\r\n 6. [#navigate's \"if matches about:blank or is about:srcdoc\" condition](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#beginning-navigation:about:srcdoc): **no**, because we cannot invoke #navigate with a URL that matches about:srcdoc that _isn't_ exactly about:srcdoc, in the non-fragment-navigation case\r\n 7. [constructing a synthetic response whose URL is about:srcdoc](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#populating-a-session-history-entry:about:srcdoc): **N/A**\r\n\r\nIf we agree on that, then I think once https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/9558 lands we can close this.",
