    "body": "I meant that it makes it to the navigate algorithm. Then, what path it goes down from there, depends on our decision to use \"is\" vs. \"matches\". If we use \"is\", we get a network error. (Like Firefox??) Whereas if we use \"matches\", I think the algorithm blows up because there's no _documentResource_? And neither of those matches Chrome, from what I can tell, and I haven't tested Safari.",
